  /// Determines whether to use the CloudWatch alarm option in the service
  /// deployment process.
  pub enable: Bool? = None
}

/// The deployment circuit breaker can only be used for services using the
/// rolling update ( ECS ) deployment type. The deployment circuit breaker
/// determines whether a service deployment will fail if the service can't
/// reach a steady state. If it is turned on, a service deployment will
/// transition to a failed state and stop launching new tasks. You can also
/// configure Amazon ECS to roll back your service to the last completed
/// deployment after a failure. For more information, see Rolling update in
/// the Amazon Elastic Container Service Developer Guide . For more
/// information about API failure reasons, see API failure reasons in the
/// Amazon Elastic Container Service Developer Guide .
pub struct DeploymentCircuitBreaker {
  /// Determines whether to use the deployment circuit breaker logic for the
  /// service.
