/// A list of files containing the environment variables to pass to a
/// container. You can specify up to ten environment files. The file must
/// have a .env file extension. Each line in an environment file should
/// contain an environment variable in VARIABLE=VALUE format. Lines
/// beginning with # are treated as comments and are ignored. If there are
/// environment variables specified using the environment parameter in a
/// container definition, they take precedence over the variables contained
/// within an environment file. If multiple environment files are specified
/// that contain the same variable, they're processed from the top down. We
/// recommend that you use unique variable names. For more information, see
/// Use a file to pass environment variables to a container in the Amazon
/// Elastic Container Service Developer Guide . Environment variable files
